    "text": "Suppose that G is a finite group and x is an element of G such that the\nsubgroup ⟨x, y⟩ has odd order for any y conjugate to x in G. Prove, without using\nCFSG, that the normal closure of x in G is a group of odd order.     L. S. Kazarin",
